From: Albrecht Lohofener <albrechtloh@gmx.de>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: use the build system's python and meson, no venv

QEMU's configure creates a Python venv and installs its vendored meson
into it. In a bitbake build the sysroot's python3-native and meson-native
are the ones to use. Combines oe-core's two qemu patches
0010-configure-lookup-meson-exutable-from-PATH.patch and
0011-qemu-Ensure-pip-and-the-python-venv-aren-t-used-for-.patch,
refreshed for QEMU 11.1.1.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific]
Signed-off-by: Albrecht Lohofener <albrechtloh@gmx.de>
---
 configure | 9 +++------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -937,14 +937,14 @@
 echo "python determined to be '$python'"
 echo "python version: $($python --version)"
 
-python="$($python -B "${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py" create pyvenv)"
+python=python3
 if test "$?" -ne 0 ; then
     error_exit "python venv creation failed"
 fi
 
 # Suppress writing compiled files
 python="$python -B"
-mkvenv="$python ${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py"
+mkvenv=true
 
 # Finish preparing the virtual environment using vendored .whl files.
 # Even if PyPI is allowed, we disallow it here to force installation
@@ -967,10 +967,7 @@
     fi
 }
 
-meson="$(cd pyvenv/bin; get_pwd)/meson"
-if [ -f "$meson$EXESUF" ]; then
-  meson="$meson$EXESUF"
-fi
+meson=`which meson`
 
 # On Haiku, meson might show up in a "non-packaged" subfolder instead, see
 # https://github.com/haiku/haiku/blob/r1beta5/docs/user/storage/storageintro.dox
